&nbsp;
<div class="bb-quote"><b>Chaosmancer wrote:</b><br /><blockquote class="bb-quote-body">I think this scenario could have been far more interesting if the halls weren&#39;t the challenge, but each room presented a challenge for the players to overcome, then at least I could have something to tell them other than &quot;find the next chamber&quot;.
&nbsp;
</blockquote></div>
&nbsp;

As GM, there&#39;s nothing stopping you from creating/making up a challenge for each of the the rooms.

Perhaps the planets in the astronomy chamber aren&#39;t properly aligned (the Egyptians wouldn&#39;t have known that the Sun is at the center of the solar system) or there are too many planets and the excess one needs to be removed? Perhaps upon entering the larder, the door closes behind the heroes and one of the vats begins emitting noxious fumes, requiring the heroes to open the correct vat and find a chemical to counteract the fume-emitting one? Maybe the long featureless hall continues endlessly in both directions no matter how far the heroes walk or run?

[/quote]

&nbsp;

I&#39;ve thought about that, it mostly works if you get rid of the twists involving getting lost, but that ends up being a major part of the scenario to change. And, man, without a move action type system, how is the failure of ending up a room behind where they started more than just a flavorful way of saying no? It doesn&#39;t end up mattering, because they can move multiple rooms a turn.

&nbsp;

This is the kind of stuff that frustrates me because I know it is me. I&#39;m making a big mental deal out of this because I&#39;m so used to systems and scenarios with very set structures, and this is not that style of game or that style of scenario. All the pieces I&#39;m used to looking at for guidance or ideas are not there, and it is perfectly fine but I&#39;m panicking because I&#39;m looking at a completely blank piece of paper with no clue how to get some vague descriptions to turn into a game plan on that sheet of paper, especially since I need to and am expected to rewrite those descriptions as I go but keep them similiar enough that the scenario still works.
